    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d310">

                <pb facs="0327" n="319" xml:id="pg319"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">852.2221/1138: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Consul at Seville</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Bay</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Seville</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1938-08-26T11:00:00+02:00">August 26, 1938—11
                        a.m.</date><lb/>[Received August 26—8:20 a.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>55. Department’s 44, August 19, 6 p.m.<anchor n="91" xml:id="d310-f1"/> Señor
                    Vidal stated over telephone last evening that if I would write him about the
                    proposal of Friends of the Abraham Lincoln Brigade he would make a reply. A
                    personal note will suffice. Instruction requested.<anchor n="92"
                        xml:id="d310-f2"/></p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Bay</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d310-f1" n="91" xml:id="d310-f1-content">
                <p>See footnote 90, <ref target="#pg318">p. 318</ref>.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d310-f2" n="92" xml:id="d310-f2-content">
                <p>Department’s telegram No. 46, August 27, 2 p.m., in reply, stated: “Personal note
                    approved.” (852.2221/1064)</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
